    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here's a slight modification of the program we previously wrote:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1def print_numbers(n):    \n2    print (n)\n3\n4    # argument is now n - 1 \n5    print_numbers(n - 1)\n6\n7print_numbers(100)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "100\n99\n98\n97\n96\n..."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, we have initially called the print_numbers() function with 100 as an argument."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In the first call (original call):"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "n is 100, which is printed.",
        "print_numbers(99) is called."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In the second call (first recursive call):"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "n is 99, which is printed.",
        "print_numbers(98) is called."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Essentially, the value of the argument is reduced by one in each subsequent function call."
    },
